   "date": "2015-06-04T00:31:57Z",
   "subject": "R Margins Too Small",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi RUG,<div>I&#39;m having trouble find the solution to this RStudio problem online.</div><div><br><div><span style=\"color:rgb(72,74,76);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:14.7727270126343px\"></span><div style=\"margin-top:5px;margin-bottom:5px;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:14.7727270126343px\"><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\">I get this error when I&#39;m trying to print graphics in R Studio:</p><pre style=\"padding:10px;font-family:Monaco,Menlo,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;border-radius:5px;margin:8px;line-height:1.25;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(198,201,204);background:-webkit-linear-gradient(top,rgb(248,248,249) 0%,rgb(236,240,243) 100%) padding-box padding-box\"><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Error</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">in</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> plot</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">new</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">()</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> figure margins too large</span></pre><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\"> </p><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\">And I can&#39;t fix it by using a function to adjust the margins:</p><pre style=\"padding:10px;font-family:Monaco,Menlo,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;border-radius:5px;margin:8px;line-height:1.25;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(198,201,204);background:-webkit-linear-gradient(top,rgb(248,248,249) 0%,rgb(236,240,243) 100%) padding-box padding-box\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">par</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mar</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">c</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">))</span></pre><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\">Graphics work fine in my regular R Console but not RStudio. Surely, there is a simple solution to this. Has anyone encountered this issue before?</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\">Thanks!</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\">Fanny Chow</p></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ySxnEv7BECwJ",
   "from": "Erica Rettig",
   "author": "4b16035cff9b0f8a",
   "date": "2015-06-04T00:39:03Z",
   "subject": "Re: [D-RUG]: R Margins Too Small",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I think it means the bottom-right window RStudio displays the graphics in is too small. Make it bigger and try again and they&#39;ll show up.<br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Jun 3, 2015 at 5:31 PM, Fanny Chow <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">fanny...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi RUG,<div>I&#39;m having trouble find the solution to this RStudio problem online.</div><div><br><div><span style=\"color:rgb(72,74,76);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:14.7727270126343px\"></span><div style=\"margin-top:5px;margin-bottom:5px;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:14.7727270126343px\"><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\">I get this error when I&#39;m trying to print graphics in R Studio:</p><pre style=\"padding:10px;font-family:Monaco,Menlo,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;border-radius:5px;margin:8px;line-height:1.25;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(198,201,204);background:-webkit-linear-gradient(top,rgb(248,248,249) 0%,rgb(236,240,243) 100%) padding-box padding-box\"><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Error</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">in</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> plot</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">new</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">()</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> figure margins too large</span></pre><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\"> </p><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\">And I can&#39;t fix it by using a function to adjust the margins:</p><pre style=\"padding:10px;font-family:Monaco,Menlo,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;border-radius:5px;margin:8px;line-height:1.25;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(198,201,204);background:-webkit-linear-gradient(top,rgb(248,248,249) 0%,rgb(236,240,243) 100%) padding-box padding-box\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">par</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mar</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">c</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">))</span></pre><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\">Graphics work fine in my regular R Console but not RStudio. Surely, there is a simple solution to this. Has anyone encountered this issue before?</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\">Thanks!</p><span><font color=\"#888888\"><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\">Fanny Chow</p></font></span></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
