  {
   "id": "AgIteor9KCIJ",
   "from": "David J. Harris",
   "author": "8d1674b7b16af1b1",
   "date": "2015-06-04T20:01:53Z",
   "subject": "Re: [D-RUG]: R Margins Too Small",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Another good option (especially if your screen still isn’t big enough to fit everything you want) is to use a different graphics device.  It can give you a bit more control over things like this.<div><br></div><div>The code below uses the PDF device, for example.</div><div><br></div><div>Dave<br><div><br></div><div><div style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-size:11px;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(79,79,79)\"># Tell R to create a PDF file that&#39;s 10x10 inches</div><div style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-size:11px;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\"><span style=\"color:#061a99\">pdf(</span>&quot;example.pdf&quot;<span style=\"color:#061a99\">,</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">width </span><span style=\"color:#061a99\">= </span><span style=\"color:#045218\">10</span><span style=\"color:#061a99\">,</span><span style=\"color:#045218\"> </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">height </span><span style=\"color:#061a99\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#045218\">10</span><span style=\"color:#061a99\">)</span></div><div style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-size:11px;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(79,79,79)\"><span style=\"color:#061a99\">plot(</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">mtcars</span><span style=\"color:#061a99\">) </span># Make a big plot that might not fit comfortably in RStudio</div><div style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-size:11px;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(79,79,79)\"><span style=\"color:#061a99\">dev.off() </span># Seal up the file so it&#39;s readable</div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On Jun 4, 2015, at 12:47 PM, Katherine Ransom &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lockhart....@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br><div><p dir=\"ltr\">Yes, Erica is right. I get this error from time to time and I just manually make the figure display window bigger with the cursor and it fixes the problem. </p>\r\n<div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Jun 3, 2015 5:39 PM, &quot;Erica Rettig&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">erica....@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br type=\"attribution\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I think it means the bottom-right window RStudio displays the graphics in is too small. Make it bigger and try again and they&#39;ll show up.<br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Jun 3, 2015 at 5:31 PM, Fanny Chow <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">fanny...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi RUG,<div>I&#39;m having trouble find the solution to this RStudio problem online.</div><div><br><div><span style=\"color:rgb(72,74,76);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:14.7727270126343px\"></span><div style=\"margin-top:5px;margin-bottom:5px;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:14.7727270126343px\"><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\">I get this error when I&#39;m trying to print graphics in R Studio:</p><pre style=\"padding:10px;font-family:Monaco,Menlo,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;border-radius:5px;margin:8px;line-height:1.25;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(198,201,204);background:-webkit-linear-gradient(top,rgb(248,248,249) 0%,rgb(236,240,243) 100%) padding-box padding-box\"><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Error</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">in</span><span> plot</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">new</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">()</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span> figure margins too large</span></pre><div style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\"> <br></div><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\">And I can&#39;t fix it by using a function to adjust the margins:</p><pre style=\"padding:10px;font-family:Monaco,Menlo,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;border-radius:5px;margin:8px;line-height:1.25;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(198,201,204);background:-webkit-linear-gradient(top,rgb(248,248,249) 0%,rgb(236,240,243) 100%) padding-box padding-box\"><span>par</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span>mar</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span>c</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">))</span></pre><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\">Graphics work fine in my regular R Console but not RStudio. Surely, there is a simple solution to this. Has anyone encountered this issue before?</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\">Thanks!</p><span><font color=\"#888888\"><p style=\"margin-bottom:2px;word-break:break-word;min-height:15px\">Fanny Chow</p></font></span></div></div></div></div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div><br></div>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nCheck out our R resources at <a href=\"http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-group.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-group.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468151827000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3LKQJswE5NH24RP4VCE_ZT\">http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-group.html</a><br>\r\n--- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Davis R Users&#39; Group&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">davis-rug+...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nVisit this group at <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468151827000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EZJuW6eSbbPOG_4AO5U_h\">http://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468151827000&amp;usg=AOvVaw288dGZwLdvowiFR8MaI-_T\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</font></span></blockquote></div><br><br clear=\"all\"><br>-- <br><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Thanks,<br></div><div>Erica</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Erica Rettig</div><div>PhD Candidate</div><div>Graduate Group in Ecology, UC Davis</div></div></div>\r\n</div><div><br></div>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nCheck out our R resources at <a href=\"http://www.noamross.net