   "subject": "Re: [D-RUG]: R Margins Too Small",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "I think Dave&#39;s advice is, as usual, excellent.  Let me add that as\r<br>another diagnostic tool you could try running your code from some\r<br>other R context, i.e., not from RStudio.  You might, for instance, use\r<br>whatever R &quot;console&quot; comes with your system, or just open a terminal\r<br>window and type &#39;R&#39;, or run the code from Emacs, etc.  This tells you\r<br>whether you have an R problem or an RStudio problem.\r<br>\r<br>-- Mike\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>On Thu, Jun 4, 2015 at 1:01 PM, David J. Harris &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">harr...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; Another good option (especially if your screen still isn’t big enough to fit\r<br>&gt; everything you want) is to use a different graphics device.  It can give you\r<br>&gt; a bit more control over things like this.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; The code below uses the PDF device, for example.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Dave\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; # Tell R to create a PDF file that&#39;s 10x10 inches\r<br>&gt; pdf(&quot;example.pdf&quot;, width = 10, height = 10)\r<br>&gt; plot(mtcars) # Make a big plot that might not fit comfortably in RStudio\r<br>&gt; dev.off() # Seal up the file so it&#39;s readable\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; On Jun 4, 2015, at 12:47 PM, Katherine Ransom &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lockhart....@gmail.com</a>&gt;\r<br>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Yes, Erica is right. I get this error from time to time and I just manually\r<br>&gt; make the figure display window bigger with the cursor and it fixes the\r<br>&gt; problem.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; On Jun 3, 2015 5:39 PM, &quot;Erica Rettig&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">erica....@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; I think it means the bottom-right window RStudio displays the graphics in\r<br>&gt;&gt; is too small. Make it bigger and try again and they&#39;ll show up.\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; On Wed, Jun 3, 2015 at 5:31 PM, Fanny Chow &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">fanny...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; Hi RUG,\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; I&#39;m having trouble find the solution to this RStudio problem online.\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; I get this error when I&#39;m trying to print graphics in R Studio:\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; Error in <a href=\"http://plot.new\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://plot.new&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468151829000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2q5SdvatElNwqJADPF7Ykl\">plot.new</a>() : figure margins too large\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; And I can&#39;t fix it by using a function to adjust the margins:\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; par(mar=c(1,1,1,1))\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; Graphics work fine in my regular R Console but not RStudio. Surely, there\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; is a simple solution to this. Has anyone encountered this issue before?\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; Thanks!\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; Fanny Chow\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; --\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; Check out our R resources at\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; <a href=\"http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-group.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-group.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468151830000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EZKLvn3EtGn8iSlLraTpa\">http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-group.html</a>\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; ---\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; &quot;Davis R Users&#39; Group&quot; group.\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">davis-rug+...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; Visit this group at <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468151830000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1P0SYtK2iGT4wrFnpYar-2\">http://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug</a>.\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; For more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" 